---
// Required closing disclaimer, written as brand-voice prose — plain, unhedged,
// unashamed — not 9px grey boilerplate. A product built on honesty owes you its
// limits in the same voice as its strengths.
---

<section class="section border-t border-line" aria-labelledby="limits-h">
  <div class="shell max-w-3xl">
    <h2 id="limits-h" class="rise mt-4 text-[clamp(1.7rem,3.5vw,2.5rem)]">
      Its limits, in the same voice as its strengths.
    </h2>
    <div class="rise mt-7 space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      <p>
        Healthee is not a medical device. It does not diagnose, treat, or prevent disease.
        Everything here is derived from consumer-wearable data and shown with its confidence &mdash;
        an estimate, never a verdict.
      </p>
      <p>
        It is not a substitute for professional care. The coach refuses medical, diagnostic, and
        emergency questions by design and points you to a clinician &mdash; not because a lawyer said
        so, but because guessing at your health would break the one promise this whole thing is built
        on.
      </p>
      <p class="text-ink">
        We tell you this in the same voice we tell you everything else: plainly. A product built on
        honesty owes you its limits as clearly as its strengths.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
